[TEXT] **Found the root cause!** Router6's iptables FORWARD chain has a critical ACL:

```
ACCEPT  TCP  in:eth2  src:172.16.10.0/24 → dst:172.18.51.1  dport:80
DROP    TCP  in:eth2  any → any
DROP    UDP  in:eth2  any → any
DROP    ALL  in:eth2  any → any    ← 24 packets already dropped (our ICMP probes!)
```

This is an ACL on router6's WAN interface (eth2 = link to router3) that **blocks ALL inbound forwarded traffic from the wider network** — killing both the return path from pc15→external and the forward path for external→172.18.51.x. The traceroute from pc15 dies at hop 1 (router6 gateway), confirming replies are dropped there.

